From 0b90853a191e2c890e27210999d1dc033767923d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kernel-rg35xx <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 21:46:50 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] atc2603c audio: RG35XX volume export, earphone poll, no
 SPDIF

What the console's own modules and speaker/headphone path need, matching
the running RG35XX kernel:
- allen_adjust_volume(write, value), exported: reads/sets the DAC PA
  volume (DAC_ANALOG1 bits 5:0); the gpio_keys_polled gamepad module on
  the rootfs calls it for the volume keys and does not load without it;
- playback controls apply that volume, digital volume 0xB5 and PA output
  swing;
- earphone_detect_method 3 (the RG35XX DTS): both detect pins
  (earphone_detect_gpios, and earphone_detect_gpios_new of the newer
  board) polled every 500 ms, h2w switch in the codec, speaker PA
  switched by the poll; poll stopped on suspend/remove, restarted on
  resume;
- speaker PA off at shutdown (the public source switched it on);
- no SPDIF: not selected by SND_SOC_ALL_PMU_OWL, no SPDIF dai link.

Not ported (no Bluetooth on this console; to revisit if audio differs):
the vendor's Bluetooth PCM card device (hw:0,2), its S900-style DAI and
PCM/DMA rework, the input-mode control and the deferred link init.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
